# D-STAT-ABORTED-BY-THE-RECOVERY-BLOCKED-CUTOFF-ENDS-ITS-INODE-DLM-HOLD-UNPAIRED:
# the verification its record wrote when the patch went in (0.87.22, s59), on
# the main tree's build (65863B924040AF5213F2A76, which carries
# XFS_ILOCK_MXFS_NOEND, xfs/xfs_inode.h, used by xfs/xfs_mxfs_fallible.c, and
# the -EHOSTDOWN arm's mxfs_acqfall_give_up_rc, xfs/xfs_mxfs_ilock.c), on the
# 2-node TCP pair g2c (2/net/mesh/direct).
#
# RULES (the record's, unchanged): each tests/d0356_stranded_prover_return.sh
# lap must print P958-GETATTR-REFUSED rc=-5 after P240-RBLK-EIO-ABORT
# comm=umount, and ZERO 'P71-UNDERFLOW.*un=mxfs_getattr_dlm_unlock' and ZERO
# 'un=mxfs_ilock_fallible' in any node's kernel log over the lap; the
# tests/tcp_lockreq_blackhole.sh lap (ARMED_S=180, on a freshly prepped mount,
# both nodes mounted) must print ZERO 'un=mxfs_ilock_fallible' where s586h
# printed them.  A d0356 lap with no P240-RBLK-EIO-ABORT comm=umount did not
# reach the abort and judges nothing; any P71-UNDERFLOW from either end site is
# NOT FIXED, attributed from its own lines.  Every lap's own harness verdict
# (PASS, both witnesses readable, platter clean) must also hold.
#
# STAGING (changed after laps sav1/sav2, both VACUOUS): this rig's SCST target
# retains a destroyed initiator's registration, so A's present-key PREEMPT AND
# ABORT proved exclusion on the first attempt and the gate refusal was never
# reached.  The harness now also arms pr_fence_inject_key_absent on A (every
# attempt classifies KEY_ABSENT_UNPROVEN, submitting nothing).  The blackhole
# lap is preceded by its own prep: a VACUOUS or failed d0356 lap leaves B
# rebooted without the module (lap sav3 ABORTed on that).
#
# Bounds: d0356 1420 s (its header: prep 300 + witnesses 10 + death 180 +
# umount 120 + boot 150 + lone mount 300 + rejoin 300 + captures 60); prep 300
# (run.sh prep_cluster, measured 88-99 s on g2c); blackhole 370 s (its header:
# setup 8 x 13 + ARMED_S 180 + recovery 60 + captures 20).
#
# Run sva (06:51-07:09Z): sav4 and sav5 met the record's markers (P240 comm=umount
# then P958 rc=-5; zero P71-UNDERFLOW and zero un=mxfs_ilock_fallible in every
# journal) but their harness verdicts FAILed one check each: the returning node,
# bootstrap owner after a total outage, adopted a certified victim slot as its
# own log (P-BOOT-ADOPT rc=0, P-BOOT-ADOPTED-LOG; B's old slot in sav4, A's in
# sav5), which prints no P163-RECOVERY-COMPLETE.  The harness now counts such an
# adoption as that slot's recovery once the mount completed; the two d0356 laps
# are rerun for the harness's own verdict.  sav6 (blackhole): harness fails=0,
# zero un=mxfs_ilock_fallible; one P71-UNDERFLOW at a third site
# (un=mxfs_dlm_open_protect), outside this record's two sites, filed as
# D-ABANDONED-ACQUIRE-UNPAIRED-DLM-END-AT-OPEN-AND-UNFLAGGED-SITES.
#1420 MXFS_GROUP=g2c MXFS_CONFIG=2/net/mesh/direct tests/d0356_stranded_prover_return.sh sav4
#1420 MXFS_GROUP=g2c MXFS_CONFIG=2/net/mesh/direct tests/d0356_stranded_prover_return.sh sav5
#300 MXFS_FORCE_PREP=1 ./run.sh 2/net/mesh/direct --group g2c prep_cluster
#370 ARMED_S=180 tests/tcp_lockreq_blackhole.sh sav6 test30 test29
1420 MXFS_GROUP=g2c MXFS_CONFIG=2/net/mesh/direct tests/d0356_stranded_prover_return.sh sav7
1420 MXFS_GROUP=g2c MXFS_CONFIG=2/net/mesh/direct tests/d0356_stranded_prover_return.sh sav8
